-- Soma Preparations — Milestone 2 sample content (original Soma questions).
-- Inserted as 'awaiting_review'. Nothing reaches students until a reviewer verifies
-- and publishes each question, then publishes the examinations.
-- Idempotent: safe to run more than once.
begin;
“Neither the director nor the officers ___ present at the meeting.”', 'With “neither … nor”, the verb agrees with the subject closer to it. Here the nearer subject is “the officers” (plural) and the sentence is in the past, so “were” is correct.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'english-communication'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
“The committee submitted ___ report on time.”', '“Its” (no apostrophe) is the possessive form: the report belongs to the committee. “It''s” means “it is”, and “its''” is not a word.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'english-communication'), 'foundation', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?', 'The differences between terms are 4, 6, 8 and 10, increasing by 2 each time. The next difference is 12, so 30 + 12 = 42.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'logic-analytical-problem-solving'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
Which statement must be true?', 'Only the restated premise must be true. The two statements do not tell us whether any civil servant is a teacher, so options A, B and D cannot be concluded.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'logic-analytical-problem-solving'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
Who is the youngest?', 'From oldest to youngest the order is Pema, Karma, Dorji, Sonam. Sonam is younger than Dorji, who is younger than everyone else, so Sonam is the youngest.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'logic-analytical-problem-solving'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
What was the percentage increase?', 'Increase = 1,500 − 1,200 = 300. Percentage increase = 300 ÷ 1,200 × 100 = 25%. (20% would be 300 as a share of the 2024 figure, which is the wrong base.)', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'data-interpretation'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
How much is allocated for equipment?', 'Equipment receives 100% − 40% − 25% = 35%. 35% of Nu. 2,00,000 (two lakh) = Nu. 70,000.', (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'PE' and slug = 'data-interpretation'), 'standard', 1, 60, true, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;

Only candidates who reach the cut-off decided by the Commission, together with those exempted, may sit the Main Examination. PE marks are not carried forward because the PE is a qualifying screen rather than part of the final merit ranking. Final selection is based on the Main Examination, which assesses core competencies and subject or general knowledge in more depth. Keeping the stages separate means every qualified candidate starts the ME on an equal footing.', 150, (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'ME' and slug = 'english-general-knowledge'), 'standard', 10, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• Explain merit as selecting candidates on ability and performance rather than connections.
• Describe how the BCSE applies merit in two stages: the PE ensures a minimum standard, and the ME produces a merit ranking for final selection.
• Use accurate details: the ME combines Academic Achievement, a Written Examination and a Viva Voce (10%, 70% and 20% for most categories; 20%, 60% and 20% for B.Ed.); selection needs at least 50% in the ME, depends on merit ranking within the category and on available vacancies; ties are broken by the written-examination score, then the viva voce.
• Discuss why this supports efficiency, such as competent recruits, public trust and fairness, and acknowledge limits, since examinations cannot measure every quality and must be updated regularly.
• End with a clear conclusion.', 400, (select id from public.subjects where stage = 'ME' and slug = 'english-general-knowledge'), 'standard', 20, 'original', 'awaiting_review') on conflict (id) do nothing;
